# Idol authority router

Start every substantive session at `AGENTS.md`, then follow its chain to
`docs/spec/constitution.md` (sole semantic law). `CLAUDE.md`,
`docs/spec/source.md`, `docs/spec/host.md` (host/shell/capability closure),
`docs/spec/AUTHORITY.md`, `docs/bootstrap.md`, `.agents/AGENT_CANONICAL.md`,
`.agents/AGENT_COORDINATION.md`, and `.agents/RELEASE_READINESS.md` are
projections only.

**Idol** (`idol`, `.id`) is the language identity. Active development is
**`clpi/duo`**. **`idollang/idol`** is the future release repository only; do
not migrate development there. Historical Idol, Duo, Duon, `.id`, and `duo`
bootstrap names are provenance only.

Run `./tools/node/dev/orient` and `./tools/node/dev/doctor` before substantive
work. Identify the semantic owner and bounded boundary before editing. Prefer
deletion or convergence over new mechanisms. Do not restore historical
architecture or duplicate MCP manifests, emitters, or coordination ledgers.
